{
  "requirement": "`habeas mdbook` MUST NOT generate per-test coverage subchapters or captured-source\npages under the execution-coverage chapter of\n{cite}`requirements.test-coverage.index`. File-notes pages supporting coverage\ngap explanations under {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.index.file_map.notes`\nMUST remain available.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.test-coverage.index.details`. I did not request implementation source. The reviewed tests cover both obligations from the requirement text.\n\n**Obligation 1: no per-test coverage subchapters and no captured-source pages under the execution-coverage chapter.**\n- `src/execution_coverage/book.rs#mod[tests]/fn[gaps_omit_test_data_and_preserve_saved_profiles_and_sources]` records two tests (\"one\" and \"two\") with a child process. It calls `populate` and then loops over every chapter in the resulting book. For each chapter it asserts the absence of these strings:\n  - \"Test process coverage\"\n  - \"Captured source\"\n  - \"habeas-coverage-test\"\n  - \"Test runs and provenance\"\n  - \"application/json\"\n  - \"habeasRenderCoverage\"\n  - \"binary / one\"\n  - \"binary / two\"\n  - the captured source text `fn passing() {}`\n- The same loop asserts that no chapter name starts with \"binary /\" and that no chapter path ends with `-source.md`.\n- It asserts that every chapter is either \"Coverage gaps\" or named \"File notes:...\". A stray per-test or source subchapter would fail this check.\n- `fn[gaps_union_process_locations_and_omit_per_test_reports]` repeats the check on a separate fixture. After `populate`, every chapter after the index must have a name starting with \"File notes:\". It also asserts that the rendered HTML has no `habeas-coverage-test`, \"Test runs and provenance\", \"binary / one\" or `<select`.\n- `fn[generated_reports_inherit_the_requirements_index_hierarchy]` covers the placement case. It uses a numbered parent and an unnumbered parent. It checks the sub-items under the generated coverage chapter, and the parent has exactly 2 sub-items.\n- `fn[filtered_runs_union_latest_attempts_and_invalidate_with_saved_source]` is also marked for this requirement. It covers the multi-attempt, filtered, stale and failed cases. It only partly checks the omission obligation, but the first two tests already cover it.\n\n**Obligation 2: file-notes pages MUST remain available.**\n- `fn[gaps_union_process_locations_and_omit_per_test_reports]` computes the notes path for `code.rs`. It asserts that the file card links to that path. It finds the chapter at that path and asserts that its content contains `File: <code>code.rs</code>`.\n- In `fn[gaps_omit_test_data_and_preserve_saved_profiles_and_sources]`, the loop requires every remaining chapter to be \"Coverage gaps\" or \"File notes:...\". It also asserts that a fully covered file gets no notes page. That is consistent with the cited `requirements.test-coverage.index.file_map.notes`, which applies to listed files.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none. The tests would reject plausible violations: per-test pages, `-source.md` pages, and removal of the notes pages. There are no acknowledgments, and none are needed.",
